# Local IPOs: a company whose headquarters is lost moves to another business of its kind; with
# nowhere to go, its price falls for the grace period (3 days here, 90 in play) and then it
# closes and the city is paid the last price. The buildings themselves are not touched: the
# scenario only treats them as lost. Everything listed is removed in cleanup.
name local ipos: a company that loses its headquarters moves, or closes after its grace period
local-ipos on
ipo-forget
ipo-healthy-days 1
ipo-grace 3
ipo-scan
ipo-list-now
ipo-first-day
expect-company trading listed
ipo-buy 10
ipo-lose-home
expect-company-home moved
expect-company trading listed
expect-log lost its headquarters (building
expect-log ) and moved to
ipo-lose-home nowhere
expect-company-home lost
expect-log no business of its kind can take it; it closes in 3 days
run-days 4
expect-company gone unlisted
expect-log closed with no headquarters at
expect-log for 10 share(s)
cleanup:
ipo-remove-test
local-ipos restore
